The Heap Mine's web page runs the story in Quixe, a Glulx interpreter in
JavaScript, with GlkOte for its display. These files are the copies Inform
10.1.2 writes into a web release, unmodified:

  quixe.min.js, glkote.min.js, dialog.css, glkote.css, resourcemap.js
      Quixe and GlkOte, copyright Andrew Plotkin, MIT licence.
      https://github.com/erkyrath/quixe
      https://github.com/erkyrath/glkote

  jquery-1.12.4.min.js
      jQuery 1.12.4, copyright the jQuery Foundation and other contributors,
      MIT licence. https://jquery.org/license/

heapmine.gblorb.js is not third-party: it is The Heap Mine itself, the
compiled story base64-encoded for Quixe, written by `./build.sh release`.
